<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palmyrene Empire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Palmyrene Empire was a breakaway state centred on the Syrian city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palmyra">Palmyra</a>, which controlled much of the Roman East in about 270–273 CE under Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zenobia">Zenobia</a>. It arose during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crisis-of-the-third-century">Crisis of the Third Century</a>, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> fragmented into three competing polities. Emperor Aurelian reconquered it in 272–273 CE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palmyrene-empire.jpg" alt="Palmyrene Empire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ennomus · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empire_of_Palmyra.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
